===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷeyh₃-}}
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:quyk|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|quik}}, {{m|enm|quic||living, alive, active}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cwic||alive}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kwiku||alive, lively quick}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kwikwaz||alive, lively, quick}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*gʷih₃wós||alive}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gʷeyh₃-||to live}}, {{m|ine-pro|*gʷeyh₃w-|t=to live}}. For semantic development, compare {{m|en|lively}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|kwik}}, {{m|nl|kwiek||lively, quick}}, {{cog|de|keck||sassy, cheeky}}, {{cog|da|kvik||lively, quick-witted, quick}}, {{m|da|kvæg||cattle}}, {{cog|fo|kvikur||quick}}, {{cog|is|kvikur||lively, quick}}, {{cog|nrn|kvikk}}, {{m|nrn|hwikk||living, swarming, teeming}}, {{cog|no|kvikk||quick, lively, quick-witted}}, {{cog|sv|kvick||quick, witty}}, and also (from Indo-European) with {{cog|el|βίος||life}}, {{cog|la|vivus||alive}}, {{cog|lt|gývas||alive}}, {{cog|lv|dzīvs||alive}}, {{cog|ru|живо́й||alive, lively, quick}}, {{cog|pl|żywy||alive}}, {{cog|cy|byw||alive}}, {{cog|ga|beo||alive}}, {{m|ga|biathaigh||to feed}}, {{cog|kmr|jîn||to live}}, {{m|kmr|jiyan||life}}, {{m|kmr|giyan||soul}}, {{m|kmr|can||soul}}, {{cog|sa|जीव||alive}}, {{cog|sq|nxit||to urge, stimulate}}. {{doublet|en|jiva}}.

