# Occurring in a short time; happening or done rapidly.
#: {{syn|en|ready}}
#: {{ux|en|That was a '''quick''' meal.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Zachary Small|title=Video Games Let Them Choose a Role. Their Transgender Identities Flourished.|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/27/arts/transgender-nonbinary-gamers.html|date=2023-12-27|passage=Veronica Ripley, 32, often speaks to friends about the role that video games played in her trans awakening: “I would try to explain it away, saying that I was playing the girl character because she had a smaller hitbox or '''quicker''' kill animations,” she said, referring to in-game advantages.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201015155/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/27/arts/transgender-nonbinary-gamers.html}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Genevieve Ko|title=‘This Is the Best Dish I Have Ever Made From NYT Cooking’|date=2026-03-15|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/15/dining/this-is-the-best-dish-i-have-ever-made-from-nyt-cooking.html|passage=The importance of Nowruz is reflected in an elaborate sabzi polo, the herbed rice capped with a crunchy tahdig, the crust formed from lettuce, rice mixed with yogurt or lavash or another thin flatbread. On Wednesday night, I opted for sheveed polo, a simpler and '''quicker''' dill rice, but I can’t wait to nail that crunchy tahdig tonight.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/Obwer|archivedate=2026-03-15}}
# {{U|lively}}, fast-thinking, [[witty]], [[intelligent]].
#: {{ux|en|You have to be very '''quick''' to be able to compete in ad-lib theatrics.}}
# Mentally [[agile]], [[alert]], [[perceptive]].
#: {{ux|en|My father is old but he still has a '''quick''' wit.}}
# {{lb|en|of people or tempers}} Easily [[arouse]]d to [[anger]]; [[quick-tempered]].
#: {{ux|en|She has a very '''quick''' temper.}}
#: {{ux|en|He is wont to be rather '''quick''' of temper when tired.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1549|author=w:Hugh Latimer|title=The Sixth Sermon Preached Before King Edward, April 6 1549
|passage=The bishop was somewhat '''quick''' with them, and signified that he was much offended.}}
# {{senseid|en|alive living}}{{lb|en|archaic}} [[alive|Alive]], [[living]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|2 Timothy|4|1|page=1455|column=2|passage=I charge thee therefore before God, and the Lord Ieſus Chriſt, who ſhall iudge the '''quicke''' and the dead at his appearing, and his kingdome:}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1633|author=w:George Herbert|title=The Temple
|passage=Man is no star, but a '''quick''' coal / Of mortal fire.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1874|author=[[w:James Thomson (B.V.)|James Thomson]]|title=[[:w:City of Dreadful Night|The City of Dreadful Night]]|section=X
|passage=The inmost oratory of my soul,<br>Wherein thou ever dwellest '''quick''' or dead,<br>Is black with grief eternal for thy sake.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|of a foetus}} At the stage where it can be felt to move in the [[uterus]].
#* {{rfdate|en}} Section 316, [https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/PC1871 Penal Code (Cap. 224, 2008 Ed.) (Singapore)]
#*: Whoever does any act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide, and does by such act cause the death of a '''quick''' unborn child, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
# {{lb|en|now|rare|archaic}} [[pregnant|Pregnant]], especially at the stage where the foetus's movements can be felt; figuratively, alive with some emotion or feeling.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Love's Labour's Lost|V|ii|passage=she's '''quick'''; the child brags in her belly already: tis yours}}
#* {{RQ:Roethke Collected|Death Piece|4|Invention sleeps within a skull<br>No longer '''quick''' with light,<br>The hive that hummed in every cell<br>Is now sealed honey-tight.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author={{w|Jerry White (historian)|Jerry White}}|title=London in the Eighteenth Century|publisher=Bodley Head|year_published=2017|page=385
|passage=When sentenced she sought to avoid hanging by declaring herself with child – ironically, given her favourite deception – but a ‘jury of Matrons’ found her not '''quick'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|of water}} [[flowing|Flowing]], not [[stagnant]].
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[burning|Burning]], [[flammable]], [[fiery]].
#* {{RQ:Eddison Worm|page=18|passage=And it seemed to me that the dream smote the roof above my bed, and the roof opened and disclosed the outer dark, and in the dark travelled a bearded star, and the night was '''quick''' with fiery signs.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[fresh|Fresh]]; [[bracing]]; [[sharp]]; [[keen]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Pericles|IV|i|47|passage={{...}} the ayre is '''quicke''' there, / And it perces and ſharpens the ſtomacke,}}
# {{lb|en|mining|of a [[vein]] of [[ore]]}} [[productive]]; not "[[dead]]" or [[barren]]
# {{lb|en|crosswording}} Not [[cryptic]].
# Being a distinctively [[sensitive]] kind of [[glaciomarine]] [[clay]] that may behave like a watery fluid under stress.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022|author=Anna Bondo Medhus; Lone Klinkby|title=Engineering Geophysics|page=227
|passage=Note that '''quick''' clay is a subet of brittle material; all '''quick''' clay is brittle, but not all brittle clay is '''quick'''.) Glaciomarine clay turns into '''quick''' clay after extensive pore water leaching by ground- and rainwater.}}

